kosha selection

  -- relational algebra selection: σ_P(R) — filter rows by predicate P.
  -- the most frequent pattern in tantras (168 occurrences):
  --   graph | where [s, e, o] | and (eq e "satya") | collect s
  -- is exactly σ_{e="satya"}(π_s(G)).
  -- pure: no state, no side effects. composes freely.

  "algebra-varga-karma"
  "morphism-swarupa function-sthita"
  "partial-order-sthita"
  "set-sthita"
  "predicate-janya relation-janya"
  "subset-phala"

  shabda selection, filter, sigma / relational-algebra-selection-filter-rows-of-a-relation-by-predicate

done
